<title>USA: Cray Research seeks to speed dumping ruling.</title>
<headline>Cray Research seeks to speed dumping ruling.</headline>
<dateline>EAGAN, Minn. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cray Research Inc said Wednesday it is seeking to speed action on its antidumping complaint against a competitor by intervening in a lawsuit designed to thwart its complaint.</p>
<p>The Silicon Graphics Inc subsidiary said a suit by NEC Corp is trying prevent the U.S. Department of Commerce from investigating a dumping complaint filed against NEC by Cray. Cray said it has petitioned the Court of International Trade for permission to intervene in the lawsuit NEC and its U.S. subsidiary, HNSX Supercomputers Inc, filed against the Department of Commerce.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seeking to intervene in this action to help speed the resolution of our antidumping complaint,&quot; said Cray Research president Robert Ewald.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
